# "When Ojer Pakpatiq dies, return it to the battlefield tapped and transformed under its owner's control with three time
# counters on it" (CR 712.14a, 122.6), and Temple of Cyclical Time: "{T}: Add {U}. Remove a time counter from this land." and
# "{2}{U}, {T}: Transform this land. Activate only if it has no time counters on it and only as a sorcery."
# Bot1 casts Ojer Pakpatiq on turn 1 (Mox Sapphire, Island, Mox Pearl, Mox Jet) and Bot2 kills it with a Lightning Bolt on turn
# 2: it returns as a new object (CR 400.7), the Temple, tapped, with three time counters. Bot1 taps it for {U} on turns 3, 5 and
# 7, each time one counter fewer (2, 1, 0). Turn 5 and turn 7: refused, with the Moxen's mana to pay, while it has a counter on it
# (turn 5) and, at none, while it is tapped (turn 7); in the turn 9 upkeep, untapped and at none, refused again: only as a
# sorcery (CR 602.5d). Turn 9, main phase: transformed, paid with the three Moxen, back into Ojer
# Pakpatiq (CR 701.27c: the same permanent), tapped by the cost.

